1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:03,040
Hi everyone. If you haven't yet seen our

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,040
video on recurrent schedules and the one

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,550
diving into custom recurrent feature,

4
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:08,800
[music] I recommend watching them first.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,480
They cover the setting up tasks to

6
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,639
repeat automatically. In this video,

7
00:00:12,639 --> 00:00:14,400
we'll focus on how updating recurrent

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,240
schedules works with two important

9
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:19,359
aspects, replacing and deleting. [music]

10
00:00:19,359 --> 00:00:21,359
These options give you more control when

11
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:23,920
managing your recurrent schedules. Let's

12
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,400
start with replace. Imagine you've set

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,199
up a task to repeat every day. Later you

14
00:00:29,199 --> 00:00:31,599
decide you only want it on Friday,

15
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:34,239
Saturday [music] and Sunday.

16
00:00:34,239 --> 00:00:36,719
Here you can see the parent task. Open

17
00:00:36,719 --> 00:00:38,800
the expanded menu and click update

18
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,000
recurring. [music]

19
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,640
Let's set the custom recurrent schedule

20
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:46,160
every one week, Friday, Saturday,

21
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,920
Sunday. [music]

22
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,440
Now you can see the option replace

23
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,920
existing tasks. Choosing this will reset

24
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:54,000
the recurring schedule and only keep the

25
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,039
new days you've selected. This way your

26
00:00:57,039 --> 00:00:58,399
schedule stays clean and [music]

27
00:00:58,399 --> 00:01:00,960
accurate. If you haven't selected the

28
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,199
replace existing tasks option, all the

29
00:01:03,199 --> 00:01:05,439
child task we already had would stay

30
00:01:05,439 --> 00:01:07,119
while the recurrent schedule would get

31
00:01:07,119 --> 00:01:09,840
updated. So you would have both the old

32
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,720
child tasks and the new ones. Now what

33
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,159
if you want to remove the scheduled

34
00:01:14,159 --> 00:01:16,159
tasks altogether? [music]

35
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,320
You have two choices. You can delete

36
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:21,439
tasks manually or you can simply update

37
00:01:21,439 --> 00:01:23,280
the schedule itself to the no repeat

38
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,400
option. [music]

39
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,040
So again click update recurring and

40
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:29,360
select no repeat. [music]

41
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,600
Now you'll see the delete existing tasks

42
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,000
option. This removes the recurring

43
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,720
schedule completely and leaves the task

44
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:38,880
as a single item in your list. [music]

45
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,560
If we haven't selected the delete

46
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:42,720
existing tasks option, all the child

47
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,520
task would stay as individual tasks.

48
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,960
There is also something important to

49
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:48,960
know about detaching schedules. [music]

50
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,880
If you remove a recurring schedule, it

51
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,720
detaches a parent task from its child

52
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:55,680
tasks. Then if you later create a new

53
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:57,680
schedule for that same task, the replace

54
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,840
option won't appear anymore. [music]

55
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,759
Instead, the system will simply add new

56
00:02:01,759 --> 00:02:04,079
entries alongside the old ones, which

57
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:06,240
can lead to duplicates.

58
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,726
Why have we designed it this way?

59
00:02:07,726 --> 00:02:09,520
[music] Because if you've already

60
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:12,160
customized those child tasks by renaming

61
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,931
them, setting time estimates, or adding

62
00:02:14,931 --> 00:02:17,040
[music] notes, we don't want an update

63
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,520
to override all of your changes. This

64
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,440
approach gives you two different options

65
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,520
depending on your needs. either keep all

66
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:25,840
of your schedule tasks intact or start

67
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:28,160
fresh with a new schedule. [music]

68
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:29,599
We keep working on improving this

69
00:02:29,599 --> 00:02:31,840
feature, so be sure to subscribe to the

70
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,239
channel to not miss any updates. [music]

71
00:02:34,239 --> 00:02:36,319
I hope this clears up how updating the

72
00:02:36,319 --> 00:02:38,640
current schedules works in Blitz. If

73
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:40,160
this video was helpful, [music] check

74
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,160
out our other tutorials and join the

75
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,080
Blitz Discord community where you can

76
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,680
connect with other productivity-driven

77
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:50,040
users. Happy Blitzing.